cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it and the manuscript it accompanies."
type: software
title: "Code, conditions and aggregate results of 'Per-person sequence models of keystroke behaviour: what remains of the gain against stronger comparisons'"
abstract: >-
  Per-person sequence models of keystroke behaviour compared, on each writer's later sessions, with a shared model of
  the same structure and with the writer's own first-order Markov chain, on public co-writing (CoAuthor) and
  programming (CS1) keystroke data coded per second over overlapping 30-second windows.
  The archive holds the symbolization kit with per-record hashes of the symbols, the fitting and evaluation code of
  four analyses and twelve later checks, the conditions committed before each computation (in Japanese, with an
  English summary), the aggregate and synthetic results, checks of the SHA-256 records, and the manuscript sources.
  The data and per-writer values of real writers are not included.
